<body>
<abstractGroup>
<abstract>
<p>We conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis of pharmacokinetic studies of <bold>direct oral anticoagulants</bold> (DOACs) in patients with varying degrees of renal impairment.</p>
</abstract>
</abstractGroup>
<section>
<title>Introduction</title>
<p>DOACs are increasingly used as alternatives to warfarin for thromboembolic disease prevention. However, all DOACs undergo some degree of renal elimination, raising concerns about drug accumulation in <italic>chronic kidney disease</italic> (CKD).</p>
</section>
<section>
<title>Results</title>
<section>
<title>Pharmacokinetic Parameters</title>
<tabular>
<label>Table 1</label>
<title>AUC fold-change relative to normal renal function (eGFR &gt;80)</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="5">
<thead>
<row><entry>Drug</entry><entry>Renal Elim. (%)</entry><entry>Mild (50–80)</entry><entry>Moderate (30–50)</entry><entry>Severe (&lt;30)</entry></row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row><entry>Dabigatran</entry><entry>80</entry><entry>1.5×</entry><entry>3.2×</entry><entry>6.3×</entry></row>
<row><entry>Rivaroxaban</entry><entry>36</entry><entry>1.1×</entry><entry>1.6×</entry><entry>2.0×</entry></row>
<row><entry>Apixaban</entry><entry>27</entry><entry>1.2×</entry><entry>1.3×</entry><entry>1.4×</entry></row>
<row><entry>Edoxaban</entry><entry>50</entry><entry>1.3×</entry><entry>1.7×</entry><entry>2.1×</entry></row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</tabular>
</section>
<section>
<title>Dose Adjustments</title>
<p>Based on the pharmacokinetic data, we propose the following dose modifications:</p>
<tabular>
<label>Table 2</label>
<title>Recommended dose adjustments in renal impairment</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="4">
<thead>
<row><entry>Drug</entry><entry>Standard Dose</entry><entry>Moderate CKD</entry><entry>Severe CKD</entry></row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row><entry>Dabigatran</entry><entry>150 mg BID</entry><entry>110 mg BID</entry><entry>Contraindicated</entry></row>
<row><entry>Rivaroxaban</entry><entry>20 mg QD</entry><entry>15 mg QD</entry><entry>Avoid</entry></row>
<row><entry>Apixaban</entry><entry>5 mg BID</entry><entry>5 mg BID</entry><entry>2.5 mg BID</entry></row>
<row><entry>Edoxaban</entry><entry>60 mg QD</entry><entry>30 mg QD</entry><entry>30 mg QD</entry></row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</tabular>
</section>
</section>
<section>
<title>Conclusions</title>
<p>Apixaban demonstrates the most favorable pharmacokinetic profile in CKD due to its <bold>low renal dependence</bold>. Dabigatran should be avoided in severe renal impairment.</p>
</section>
